# Parent component: establishes a parent-child relationship between entities.
# The parent may be missing or dead; in that case the edge is inactive and the
# child evaluates as unparented until the target becomes live. Self-parenting is
# illegal. The complete live ChildOf graph MUST be acyclic, including across
# allocators. Proactive whole-graph cycle detection is OPTIONAL, but every graph
# traversal MUST be cycle-safe or resource-bounded. A peer that detects a cycle
# MAY terminate its participation in the session. Deleting a parent leaves the
# stored dead reference inactive; it does not mutate children owned by peers.
#
# Changing this component has keep-local semantics: TransformComponent and
# TransformSampleComponent numeric values are not converted, and are interpreted
# in the new effective parent frame. Reparenting clears transform sample history;
# the retained current sample becomes the first sample in that new frame.

from "../../common.jaw" use {EntityID}

pack ChildOfComponent
- parent : EntityID # parent entity identifier
